  "method": "Read-only source comparison and execution-free Mono.Cecil IL inspection; no native installed file access, game execution, attachment, or source modification.",
  "findings": [],
  "observedFailure": "r8 reported zero combat casualties despite successful full population, allocator exhaustion, and 64-slot reuse. This review does not claim the missing alarm/target calls were the experimentally established cause.",
  "acceptedChange": [
    "Combat starts only after full-population, exhaustion and exact 64-slot reuse acceptance.",
    "IssueCombatOrders reapplies Charge and sets Alarmed plus live opposing-side targets using stable spawn-position ordering. All target agents are selected from IsActive snapshots. Player position zero is excluded from AI command mutation.",
    "Modulo assignment is guarded by enemies.Length > 0. Sorting each side avoids the previous all-pairs nearest-target scan.",
    "No health reduction, direct damage, forced casualty, acceptance weakening, or native API exposure was introduced.",
    "Movement and damage counts are diagnostic snapshots of currently active agents; they are not cumulative activity counts or substitute acceptance.",
    "Five-second recycling reports preserve the original callback wait and timeout.",
    "Combat casualty and full staged teardown requirements remain mandatory."
  ],
  "managedFindings": [
    "Mission constructor initializes AllowAiTicking to true.",
    "AgentHumanAILogic.OnAgentCreated adds HumanAIComponent to AI-controlled human agents.",
    "Official Mission.SpawnTroop explicitly alarms AI agents when requested after calling SpawnAgent; raw SpawnAgent has no direct SetWatchState/SetAlarmState call.",
    "WatchState.Alarmed=2 maps through CurrentWatchState setter to SetAlarmState flag3.",
    "SetTargetAgent forwards the native agent pointer and target agent index through IMBAgent; null would be -1 but this correction only passes selected active targets."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Correct combat behavior remains to be verified by r9 runtime; r8 did not capture watch-state, target, movement or damage telemetry.",
    "This review does not prove navmesh quality, target reachability, all agents fighting, or a minimum battlefield frame rate.",
    "Official SpawnTroop can also wield initial weapons; prior layered probe and corrected probe use alarm/target APIs without that explicit helper. No additional setup is asserted necessary without runtime evidence.",
    "Managed AI commands can retain native targets until the next periodic refresh; this is standard Agent API use, not a new native pointer lifetime guarantee."
  ],
